# Model & Experiment Rules

All models and training are Python/PyTorch. See `docs/MODEL_PLAN.md` and
`docs/EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.md`.

## Main model: CAP-EEGNet (Confidence-aware Prototype EEGNet)

Components:
- EEGNet encoder (backbone).
- Adapter (lightweight, for target fine-tuning + online adaptation).
- Classification head.
- Prototype head (global + subject + session prototypes; distance/margin).
- Confidence head (multi-source: predictive entropy, prototype margin, consistency,
  calibration — NOT just softmax max prob).

Baselines (EEGNet/DeepConvNet/FBCNet) are OPTIONAL and not the current priority.

## Tensor convention

- Dataset returns `X` as `[channels, time]` (58 x 1000), `y` scalar in {0,1}.
- DataLoader batches `[batch, channels, time]`; the model adds the singleton
  `[batch, 1, channels, time]` internally.

## Main experiment: 41/10 cross-subject pretraining

- Split by SUBJECT (41 source / 10 target). Never trial-wise. No target leakage.
- Train CAP-EEGNet on all 3 sessions of the 41 source subjects.
- Zero-shot test on all 3 sessions of the 10 target subjects.
- Persist each split to `splits/<name>.json`; repeat over seeds; report mean +/- std.

## Fine-tuning

- From the pretrained model, per target subject: fine-tune on Session 1, test on
  Session 2 + 3. Compare zero-shot / classifier-only / adapter / prototype / full.

## Losses & metrics

- Classification (CE) + prototype margin + confidence calibration (+ optional
  consistency / domain).
- Report Accuracy, Balanced Accuracy, Macro-F1, AUC; plus ECE/NLL/Brier and
  risk-coverage for the confidence head.

## Run hygiene

- Fixed seeds. Every run saves resolved config + split + checkpoint + metrics + logs
  under a unique `run_id` in `outputs/` and `checkpoints/`. Never overwrite without a
  new `run_id`. All hyperparameters via YAML configs. GPU work via Slurm only.
- Do NOT build the full CAP-EEGNet / training loop yet — current stage is data/paths.
  Keep model code as documented skeletons until preprocessing is finalized.
